      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below $a_{23}=-3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}+2R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{3}:=R_{3}-3R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}+2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3}-3R_{2}$.",
